  "final_agent_text": "READY_TO_MODEL\n\nConfirmed understanding:\n\n- **Objective:** Minimize total pollution generated by all trips.\n- **Decision variables:**\n  - Number of trips for each method (horse, bicycle, handcart) — non-negative integers.\n  - Amount of produce carried on each trip — non-negative, can be fractional (pending internal confirmation, but treated as continuous for now), bounded above by the method's per-trip capacity.\n- **Constraints:**\n  1. Total produce carried across all trips ≥ 1000 units.\n  2. Total pollution ≤ 1000 units.\n  3. Horse trips ≥ 8 (minimum, not fixed).\n  4. At most one of {bicycle, handcart} may be used (i.e., if bicycle trips > 0 then handcart trips = 0, and vice versa; both can be 0).\n  5. Per-trip capacity: each trip by a method carries at most that method's capacity (horse ≤ 55, bicycle ≤ 30, handcart ≤ 40).\n  6. Pollution per trip: horse = 80, bicycle = 0, handcart = 0. Total pollution = 80 × (number of horse trips).\n- **Notes:**\n  - The horse can carry less than 55 units on some trips.\n  - Bicycle/handcart can carry less than their capacity on some trips.\n  - No upper bound on total trips.\n  - Using only the horse is allowed.\n  - If bicycle or handcart is used, it can make any positive integer number of trips (no minimum).",
